        "code": {
          "text": "Cough history"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Cough for approximately 2–3 weeks, gradually worsening; mostly dry with occasional small amounts of clear/white sputum. Worse overnight and on waking, disturbing sleep most nights. No haemoptysis."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Respiratory symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Mild exertional shortness of breath, described as puffing more when walking to the letterbox. Patient reports no wheeze. No pleuritic chest pain, fever, chills, rigors, recent upper respiratory tract infection, orthopnoea, or paroxysmal nocturnal dyspnoea."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-9",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Appetite and weight"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Appetite intermittently poor since cancer treatment. Patient thinks he has lost a couple of kilograms; no regular weights available."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-10",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-10",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Gastrointestinal symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Intermittent lower abdominal discomfort and looser stools, described as longstanding. No persistent vomiting or marked abdominal distension; still passing flatus and stool. Reports sometimes seeing a little blood on the paper; this was not explored in detail. No significant rectal bleeding reported."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-11",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-11",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "General examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Thin elderly male, no acute distress, speaking in full sentences, occasional dry cough."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-12",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-12",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Respiratory examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Good air entry bilaterally with vesicular breath sounds. Faint scattered bibasal crackles, right greater than left. No focal coarse crackles, wheeze, or percussion dullness."
      }
    },
    {
